  "text": "Skip to main content\nSearch\nARTICLES BY GRADE LEVEL\nTOPICS\nANIMALS\nARTS\nASK ANGELA\nBOOKS\nBUSINESS\nCAREERS\nCOMMUNITY\nCULTURE\nDEBATE\nEARTH SCIENCE\nEDUCATION\nELECTION 2024\nENGINEERING\nENVIRONMENT\nFOOD AND NUTRITION\nGAMES\nGOVERNMENT\nHISTORY\nHOLIDAYS\nINVENTIONS\nMOVIES AND TELEVISION\nMUSIC AND THEATER\nNATURE\nNEWS\nPEOPLE\nPLACES\nPODCASTS\nSCIENCE\nSERVICE STARS\nSPACE\nSPORTS\nTHE HUMAN BODY\nTHE VIEW\nTRANSPORTATION\nWEATHER\nWORLD\nYOUNG GAME CHANGERS\nYOUR $ FINANCIAL LITERACY CONTENT\nFOR GROWN-UPS\nRESOURCE SPOTLIGHT\nLOG IN\nArticles\nK-1\n2\n3-4\n5-6\nScience\nSpotlight on Plants\nOctober 16, 2026\n\nPlants are living things. Like animals, they grow and change. Plants can move, too. They move differently from how we move. Read on to learn about plants. Plants move. Their roots move to find water. Their flowers turn toward…\n\nAudio\nSpanish\nScience\nFungus\nOctober 16, 2026\n\nFungus is a living thing. Some fungus looks like a plant. It is not. Fungus is its own group. Mold and mushrooms are two types. Fungus grows in damp places (above). Most fungi do not grow tall. But they can…\n\nAudio\nScience\nInsect Insider\nOctober 9, 2026\n\nInsects are animals. They have six legs. They have three body parts. Insects are living things. They move and eat. They grow and reproduce. Insects move. They fly or crawl. Many have wings. This is a grasshopper. Its powerful legs…\n\nAudio\nSpanish\nScience\nButterfly Changes\nOctober 9, 2026\n\nSome insects go through a big change. It is called metamorphosis. Butterflies go through metamorphosis. Here are the stages. 1. Egg An adult butterfly lays eggs (above). They will hatch in about four days. 2. Larva A larva hatches from…\n\nAudio\nScience\nAll About Animals\nOctober 2, 2026\n\nAnimals are living things. Every animal moves and grows. Every animal gets its energy from food. People are animals too. Which other animals do you know? Animals move. Animals can move by themselves. They can walk, fly, or slither. This…\n\nAudio\nSpanish\nScience\nHow Old?\nOctober 2, 2026\n\nA life span is how long a type of animal usually lives. Different animals have different lifespans. Pygmy Goby A pygmy goby (above) is a tiny fish. It has a short lifespan. The fish lives for about two months.…\n\nAudio\nScience\nIt’s Alive!\nSeptember 25, 2026\n\nLiving things are all around. Bumblebees buzz by. A bird finds a worm. Flowers bloom. These are all living things. Learn what all living things have in common. Living things move. Giraffes walk. Seals swim. Moths fly. These flowers tilt…\n\nAudio\nSpanish\nNonliving Things\nSeptember 25, 2026\n\nThe things on this page are not alive. But they have something in common with living things. Learn how they are different. Water moves. Rivers flow (above). Oceans form waves. But water is not alive. It does not move…\n\nAudio\nCommunity\nPlay Your Part\nSeptember 16, 2026\n\nPeople care for their communities. Think of the communities that you are part of. What can you do to pitch in? How can you make these communities stronger? There are lots of ways to help. Clean up. Throw away…\n\nAudio\nSpanish\nCommunity\nA Kind Community\nSeptember 16, 2026\n\nIt is easy to spread kindness. It will make your community a better place. Here are some things you can do. Which one of these will you try today? Introduce yourself. Say hi to someone new. Tell them your name.…\n\nAudio\nCommunity\nServing Communities\nSeptember 11, 2026\n\nMany people work in a community. They keep it safe and clean. They help people get the things they need. Who are the community workers in your area? Thank them for a job well done! Firefighters These men and women…\n\nAudio\nSpanish\nCommunity\nJobs at School\nSeptember 11, 2026\n\nSchool workers are important. They help the school run smoothly. Thank you, school staff! Getting to School Crossing guards (above) guide students across the street. They signal for cars to stop. They keep kids safe on their walk.…\n\nAudio\nCommunity\nIn the Community\nSeptember 4, 2026\n\nThere are different types of places in a community. They are where people can get what they need. There are places to work, to play, and to learn. Take a walk or ride around. Where can you go? Schools …\n\nAudio\nSpanish\n1 2 3 4 5 … 43 Next\nCONTACT US\nPRIVACY POLICY\nTERMS OF SERVICE\nSUBSCRIBE\nCLASSROOM INTERNATIONAL\n© 2026 TIME USA, LLC. All Rights Reserved.\nPowered by WordPress.com VIP",
